+/*
+================
+vkquake-ios overlay 0023 — R6 part A: THE DISCHARGE SIGNAL, and per-hand refire
+clocks (A1's handoff and A2).
+
+`attack_finished` is a QuakeC field, not an entvars_t member, so it is reached
+the same way host_cmd.c already reaches `ammo_shells1`: ED_FindFieldOffset by
+name, resolved once per loaded progs. A mod whose progs lacks it (none in the
+id lineage, but the guarantee is the point) simply turns both features off.
+
+WHY IT IS THE RIGHT FIELD FOR BOTH JOBS. Stock weapons.qc:
+
+    void() W_WeaponFrame =
+    {
+        if (time < self.attack_finished)  return;      <- (a)
+        ImpulseCommands ();                            <- (b)
+        if (self.button0) { SuperDamageSound(); W_Attack(); }
+    };
+
+and every W_Fire* sets `self.attack_finished = time + <refire>`. So:
+
+  * a shot LEAVING is exactly the moment that field steps forward, inside the
+    think — which is the handoff signal A1 wants, with no timer to tune (the
+    timeout in the scheduler exists for shots that can never come, not for
+    normal fire);
+  * line (a) is ALSO why one shared clock jams the other hand: while it is in
+    the future W_WeaponFrame returns before (b), so the other hand's weapon
+    switch is not merely delayed in firing, it is not even READ. Virtualising
+    the field per hand is therefore not a nicety — without it, alternating a
+    rocket launcher with a nailgun runs the nailgun at the ROCKET's rate.
+
+The edict carries exactly one hand's clock at a time; the other hand's lives in
+`vkq_vr_af_saved` and they are exchanged when the scheduler hands the pipeline
+over — the same mechanism, and the same think window, that the barrel-true
+origin shift above already uses.
