+/*
+================
+VKQ_VR_ClockReady -- overlay 0023 (R6 part A2)
+
+Can this hand's weapon fire RIGHT NOW? The scheduler asks before handing the
+pipeline over, and the answer is what stops the fair-handoff rule from becoming
+the very jam it exists to prevent: "alternate on every discharge" would hand the
+pipeline to a rocket launcher whose clock is 0.8 s out, park it there doing
+nothing until the starvation timeout expired, and throttle the nailgun to the
+rocket's rate.
+
+NAMES THE SERVER VM EXPLICITLY, and touches the ambient `qcvm` nowhere: the
+scheduler calls this from CL_AccumulateCmd, which host.c runs BEFORE the
+`PR_SwitchQCVM (&sv.qcvm)` block, so `qcvm` is NULL (or the CSQC vm) right here
+and reading `qcvm->time` would be a null dereference on the first handoff of
+every session.
+
